Where the copied files under this repository came from, and what may be done to them.

source repository   the private half of Carbon, named in that repository's README
source commit       f335fcf7ab7c1872fb0e3864917a3e9f76d9930e
copied on           2026-09-10

Copied verbatim, as whole files, with no edit of any kind:

  harness/codex/**        minus verifications/
  lib/faults.mjs          the fault shape harness/codex/ imports
  tools/lib/mcp.mjs       the MCP server scaffold the reply tool is served by
  tools/lib/fault.mjs     what mcp.mjs imports
  tools/lib/args.mjs      what mcp.mjs imports
  tools/lib/manifest.mjs  what mcp.mjs imports

Why a copy and not a dependency. The runtime process is the one thing a systemd
unit starts on a box, and it spawns the harness as its direct child, so the
harness's code has to be inside the tarball that lands there. The private
repository holds the machinery and the wisdom; what it renders goes around, and
this code is a rendering. The private repository stays the authority: its
test/public-copies.test.mjs compares these files with the ones here, byte for
byte, whenever both checkouts are present, and fails on any drift.

What is not copied. harness/codex/verifications/ and harness/README.md stay in
the private repository. They are the record of what the pinned binary actually
does and the reasoning behind the boundary, which is wisdom rather than a
rendering, and several of them name the machine the runs were made on, which
this repository's identifier scan refuses.

How to change one of these files. Change it in the private repository, land it
there, copy the file here again, and update the source commit above. An edit
made here is drift and the authority's test fails on it.
